"use strict";(self.webpackChunkpos_globalpay_doc=self.webpackChunkpos_globalpay_doc||[]).push([[608],{6431(t,e,a){a.r(e),a.d(e,{_pageData:()=>i,default:()=>l});var n=a(641);const i=JSON.parse('{"path":"/setup/admin-configuration.html","title":"Admin Gateway Configuration","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Admin Gateway Configuration","description":"Step-by-step guide to configuring the POS Global Payment Terminal Gateway inside WooCommerce Checkout settings.","sidebarPosition":2},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"setup/admin-configuration.md"}'),o={name:"admin-configuration.md"},l=(0,a(6262).A)(o,[["render",function(t,e,a,i,o,l){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="admin-gateway-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-gateway-configuration"><span>Admin Gateway Configuration</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>POS Global Payment Terminal Gateway</strong> is configured and managed directly within the native WooCommerce Checkout settings tab. This gives store administrators centralized control over payment gateway enablement, default pre-selection, payment titles, customer descriptions, test mode toggles, and Globalpay merchant account credentials.</p><hr><h2 id="accessing-gateway-settings" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#accessing-gateway-settings"><span>Accessing Gateway Settings</span></a></h2><ol><li>Log into the WordPress Administration Dashboard.</li><li>Navigate to <strong>WooCommerce → Settings</strong> in the left sidebar menu.</li><li>Click on the <strong>Payments</strong> tab.</li><li>Locate <strong>POS Global Payment Terminal Gateway</strong> in the payment providers list and click <strong>Manage</strong> (or click the gateway title link).</li></ol><p><img src="/pos-globalpay-terminal-payment/images/admin-payment-providers.png" alt="WooCommerce Payment Providers List"></p><hr><h2 id="gateway-settings-breakdown" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#gateway-settings-breakdown"><span>Gateway Settings Breakdown</span></a></h2><p>Clicking <strong>Manage</strong> opens the gateway administration form:</p><p><img src="/pos-globalpay-terminal-payment/images/admin-gateway-settings.png" alt="POS Global Payment Terminal Gateway Settings"></p><h3 id="configuration-options" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration-options"><span>Configuration Options</span></a></h3><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Option Field</th><th style="text-align:left;">Control Type</th><th style="text-align:left;">Description</th><th style="text-align:left;">Default Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Enable/Disable</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Check <code>Enable POS Global Payment Terminal Gateway</code> to make the payment gateway active and available on the POS cashier checkout screen.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Checked (<code>yes</code>)</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Default Gateway</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Check <code>Make global payment terminal as a default payment gateway for point of sale</code> to automatically pre-select this method during cashier checkout.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Checked (<code>yes</code>)</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Title</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Text Input</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enter the payment method title displayed to cashiers and customers during checkout (e.g. <code>POS Global Pay Terminal</code>).</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>POS Global Pay Terminal</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Description</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Textarea</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enter custom instructions or explanatory text shown below the title on the checkout panel.</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>Pay with your credit card or debit card.</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Test Mode</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Check <code>Enable Test Mode</code> to run in sandbox environment mode (enables testing with the UPA Emulator or test credentials).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Checked (<code>yes</code>)</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Merchant ID</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Text Input</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enter your official Globalpay Merchant Identification number provided by your payment processor.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Blank</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="wordpress-plugins-list-settings-link" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#wordpress-plugins-list-settings-link"><span>WordPress Plugins List Settings Link</span></a></h2><p>For convenience, the plugin registers a direct settings shortcut on the main WordPress Plugins screen:</p><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>Plugins → Installed Plugins</strong>.</li><li>Locate <strong>POS Globalpay Terminal Payment for WooCommerce</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Settings</strong> to navigate directly to the gateway configuration page (<code>admin.php?page=wc-settings&amp;tab=checkout&amp;section=wkposglobal_payterminal_payment_terminal</code>).</li></ol><blockquote><p><strong>Note</strong>: After making any configuration changes, click <strong>Save changes</strong> at the bottom of the form. Changes immediately update active POS cashier sessions upon panel refresh.</p></blockquote>',17)])])}]])}}]);